			<div class="content" id="post-content-2492313">
									

<p>This really, really needs a proofread. There are multiple instances of compound adjectives that aren't hyphenated, a few misspellings and uncapitalized proper nouns, and general structural awkwardness in the sentences. I can go in and fix some of the minor grammatical issues, but the author needs to do the actual proofreading/major fixes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2241 has stated that it intends to grow stronger to stop more people from dying, and this will help both it and us in this aim. Killing a man with a teleported bullet was a stroke of tactical genius from the SCP object.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The ethical commentary is heavy-handed throughout this, but this paragraph specifically is where I upvoted.</p>
<hr />
<p>Edit: I went in and hyphenated the words that needed to be hyphenated, but in reading it twice, this needs a bit of a tonal cleanup as well. A lot of the superhero subject matter and the telekinesis stuff combined with the excessive amounts of personal statements by Foundation departments and personnel is dampening any clinical tone the article had.</p>
<p>Edit 2: I'll note that I left alone the British spellings of words like favorite and whatnot when I fixed a few misspellings.</p>

