			<div class="content" id="post-content-2492324">
									

<p>This one walks a razor, but ultimately I find myself an upvote. Agree partly with psul's suggestion that the last addendum is a bit heavy handed and redundant to the rest, but I would instead suggest paring it down to just the last two entries about halting and resuming testing (including removing the bit about the exact nature of the proposed test that triggered the halt order.)</p>
<p>My upvote boils down to one thing, and I'm sure that some will downvote for the same reason that I'm upvoting: this reminds me of <a href="/scp-239">SCP-239</a>. They may rationalize it as research or containment, but somewhere inside the fallible human beings of the foundation want to see this as a second chance: This time they won't lie about what he can do, but instead teach control and discipline while also ascertaining his actual limits. They'll explain as honestly as they can in terms he can relate to what the Foundation is, what it does, and why it's important. They'll do their best to instill loyalty to the Foundation's cause. And all the while they'll try to ignore that after its all done, they'll still be holding a tiger by the tail if they don't cage it as a cub.</p>

							</div>

								
