<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;For&nbsp;your&nbsp;pleasure</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;For&nbsp;your&nbsp;pleasure</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Valdez, you're fired.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> What? No!</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Yes. Get out.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> Fi-</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Valdez, we need you. Get back in here.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> Okay, I, uh, guess I'll go ahead with these tests th-</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> You'll do nothing of the sort. Get out of here.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> Aw, okay.</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Just kidding, come back.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> Uh, alright?</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Sorry about all that. How about a hug to make up for it?</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> I don't think I should&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Come on, you afraid of hugs?</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> I&#8230; guess not.</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> That's it, bring it in here.</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> I guess this isn't so bad.</p>
<p><strong>O5 Council:</strong> Valdez?</p>
<p><strong>Valdez:</strong> Yeah?</p>
<p><em>[The O5 Council suplexes Valdez messily.]</em></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Actual&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Actual&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>On another note, though, I'm not a fan of this article. The plot that goes back and forth between &quot;Foundation doing horrible things for science&quot; and &quot;Foundation having pangs of conscience&quot;, but never rises beyond a mediocre take on either.</p>
<p>There was a strong start, but especially after the interview I was constantly confused as to why any of the Foundation personnel consider this to be okay. It's stated that they're doing it for science, but I never understand the actual benefits, and as such the situation seems awfully contrived to produce such a moral dilemma (&quot;We need X! But we can only get X by doing horrible action Y, because that's just how X works.&quot;).</p>
<p>And then I'm further confused by wondering exactly how they're doing this. Are they taking this kid out into open fields and telling him there's crime going on? Or are we building elaborate sets and pretending crime only happens within this single site? They fired a mortar at him from long range, so I guess he was just loitering outside (speaking of that, how was that not considered a huge risk to his person)? Did they push a guy down the stairs, or did they wait until someone slipped?</p>
<p>They build a bank vault, had him steal from it, and then noted that he was okay with stealing from it? How in the world is such a test even conceived of? Were they testing his morality? Are there not way less expensive ways to do that than building a bank vault?</p>
<p>And besides all of these hangups, I'm still mystified as to how testing this thing and making it more powerful is an acceptable risks. It doesn't take a genius to realize that emotional instability is a horrible sign in the superpowered killing machine you're making. Even if you want to keep developing it as a killing machine, wouldn't you want that dealt with first and foremost, so it doesn't, say, kill all of you?</p>
<p>So, it's a plot that could work, and a strong premise, but it combines tons of odd and unexplained actions with a plot that doesn't really go anywhere that previous explorations haven't. The Foundation does bad things for good reasons, sometimes. But when they do it for stupid reasons or in spite of obvious dangers, they just look like douches that like to torture kids.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

